        "original_id": "83c2ad83-2e18-5a5e-adf3-d5267221b7ef",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arshile Gorky, Eve Beglarian, Alice Mason, Emily Mason\n- Places: Ann Arbor, Michigan, New York\n- Roles: painter, composer, performer, audio producer\n- Concepts: Abstract Expressionism, abstract art, Armenian descent\n\nFacts:\n- Arshile Gorky was born as Vostanik Manoug Adoian on April 15, 1904, and he became an Armenian-American painter.\n- Arshile Gorky had a seminal influence on Abstract Expressionism.\n- Arshile Gorky influenced early abstract artist Alice Mason.\n- Alice Mason had settled in New York by 1927.\n- Eve Beglarian was born in Ann Arbor, Michigan, on July 22, 1958.\n- Eve Beglarian is a contemporary American composer, performer, and audio producer of Armenian descent.\n- Alice Mason was a painter.\n- Emily Mason's mother was Alice Mason.\n- Alice Mason was the mother of Emily Mason.\n- Arshile Gorky died on July 21, 1948.",
